# mycobot 280 — Run Commands

Quick reference for launching the simulation. Two ways: Docker or native.

---

## Native (Ubuntu 22.04 host)

### Launch the simulation

```bash
cd ~/mycobot_ws
source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
source install/setup.bash
ros2 launch mycobot_moveit_config gazebo_moveit.py
```

### Rebuild after code changes

```bash
cd ~/mycobot_ws
colcon build --symlink-install \
  --packages-select \
    mycobot_description \
    mycobot_gazebo \
    mycobot_moveit_config \
    mycobot_interfaces
source install/setup.bash
```

### Clean rebuild (when build cache breaks)

```bash
cd ~/mycobot_ws
rm -rf build/ install/ log/
colcon build --symlink-install \
  --packages-select \
    mycobot_description \
    mycobot_gazebo \
    mycobot_moveit_config \
    mycobot_interfaces
source install/setup.bash
```

### Save launch output to a file

```bash
ros2 launch mycobot_moveit_config gazebo_moveit.py 2>&1 | tee ~/launch_output.txt
```

---

## Docker

### Start the container

```bash
cd ~/RoboticArm_Workspace/docker_ws
./run.sh
```

### Inside the container — launch

```bash
cd ~/arm_ws
source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
source install/setup.bash
ros2 launch mycobot_moveit_config gazebo_moveit.py
```

### Inside the container — rebuild

```bash
cd ~/arm_ws
colcon build --symlink-install \
  --packages-select \
    mycobot_description \
    mycobot_gazebo \
    mycobot_moveit_config \
    mycobot_interfaces
source install/setup.bash
```

---

## Verification (in a second terminal, while sim is running)

```bash
# Source first
source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
source ~/mycobot_ws/install/setup.bash    # or ~/arm_ws/install/setup.bash in Docker

# Check nodes are alive
ros2 node list

# Check controllers
ros2 control list_controllers

# Check the trajectory action
ros2 action list | grep follow_joint_trajectory

# Check OMPL is loaded
ros2 param get /move_group ompl.planning_plugin
```

---

## Auto-source on every terminal (optional)

Add to `~/.bashrc`:

```bash
source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
source ~/mycobot_ws/install/setup.bash
```

Then `source ~/.bashrc` once, and future terminals are ready to launch directly.
